{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And YHWH spoke to Moses: Speak to Aaron your brother, that he not come at all times into the sanctuary</b>, etc. This passage, even though it belongs to Yom HaKippurim, was said on the very day the Tabernacle was erected. And because on that day two of Aaron's sons died on account of an entry that was unnecessary, on that very day this warning was stated to Aaron: ואל יבא בכל עת. And the reason Scripture interrupted — this passage being separated from parashat Shemini, where it mentions the death of two of Aaron's sons — and fixed it after the parashah of all the impurities, is that when it finished the parashah of all the impurities, it had still not specified whether those who enter the sanctuary, whether inadvertently or deliberately — what is their atonement, and what is the purification of the sanctuary. Therefore it specifies for you here: וכפר על הקדש. <b>בקרבתם לפני יהוה</b> — upon the golden altar, not according to the law." "<b>Before the covering that is upon the ark.</b> What does Scripture tell us by saying אשר על הארון? Because it is stated regarding the curtain: וסכות על הארון — one might think the curtain is a covering for the ark. Scripture says: אל פני הכפרת אשר על הארון — the covering is the covering for the ark, and the curtain is not a covering for the ark. <b>And he shall not die</b> — the punishment we have heard; the warning, from where? Scripture says: כי בענן אראה. כי בענן אראה — said concerning it; YHWH said to dwell in the cloud."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:42.355248175Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}